{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner stale-queue triage round three, for codex. Batch one of the 2026-08-10 security-assessment self-queue, verified by reading current main 33c29b1e rather than by inferring from the board. Rounds one and two (c80ffc83, 197b0d31) covered 3ce0674f, 80f60265, 2924b769, 88c33287, f1b42e1f, bf1f2e7b, d8044f85 and ea4eefd8; these five are new. None of them is withdrawn. Their staleness is ordinary and blocks nothing, so each is claimable exactly as written.\n\n9e337057, disable Git replacement objects. STANDS, unstarted. Neither --no-replace-objects nor GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS appears in any Go file on main. gitstore.Store.run (internal/gitstore/gitstore.go:66-70) invokes git --git-dir \u003crepo\u003e with cmd.Env = append(os.Environ(), env...), and the ref read at :317 builds its own exec.CommandContext the same way, so a refs/replace/* entry is honoured by every object read and by VerifySSHCommit at :598-602. The condition's \"including direct commands outside Store.run\" is the load-bearing part: there are two such sites in gitstore alone plus cmd/gs/main.go:1873.\n\n1e0644d1, quarantine executable Git configuration. STANDS, unstarted. Same seam, and no GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL or pinned gpg.ssh.program anywhere in production code. Signing passes only -c gpg.format=ssh -c user.signingKey (gitstore.go:273-277); verification passes only gpg.format and gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile (:598-602). An inherited user or system gitconfig setting gpg.ssh.program is therefore honoured during both commit-tree -S and verify-commit, which is the sentinel-program path the request names. The only hermetic configuration in the tree is a test fixture, internal/docset/examples_test.go:124-125.\n\nad03064d, live participant membership. Work is real, filed and unlanded; do not re-file it and do not review the head it names. Your report says ready-for-review, and the fold has no author-membership gate on main: fold.go:541 refuses a request whose addressee is not live, and nothing checks the author's own standing for a statement, artifact, report or assert. The implementation is on request/live-membership-authority (103ccd47, changes-requested and ratified) and request/live-membership-authority-v2 (bbee4a4d, pushed, answering that verdict). bbee4a4d is one commit off an old base, git merge-tree against main 33c29b1e reports a conflict, and all four of its artifacts are retired, one of them at the comma-joined pseudo-path internal/workroom,internal/app,docs/reference.md. So it cannot be approved or merged as it stands. What it needs is a re-cut of bbee4a4d onto current main with fresh artifacts at the real paths, then an independent review.\n\n7d3d5728, bound resident dedup and checkpoint memory. HALF LANDED, half stands. Dedup entries are payload-free on both cache paths (kernel.go:928 and checkpoint.go:546 store eventWithoutPayload), and serialization is bounded by checkpointLimitWriter against maxCheckpointBytes and maxCheckpointManifest. The retry half is not fixed, and is worse than the request states. checkpointDue is depth-lastAttempt \u003e= 256 (checkpoint.go:1104-1106). maybeWriteCheckpoint advances checkpointAttempt only on success (kernel.go:912-925), so after one failure the due test stays true and every subsequent append re-attempts a full checkpoint write, tree, signed commit, signature verification and ref update. The rebuild path arms the same loop deliberately: on failure it sets checkpointAttempt = depth - checkpointInterval (kernel.go:891), which makes the next single append due. checkpointFailures is counted and never consulted.\n\n96cfd390, bound live sessions, conversations, frames, waiters, request bodies and HTTP connection lifetime. SUBSTANTIALLY LANDED, one residual. internal/nexus/nexus.go:42-54 declares the count and byte quotas and :430-440 enforces MaxLiveSessions and MaxSessionsPerActor; request bodies are bounded at internal/service/server.go:762 by a 2 MiB MaxBytesReader. The residual is connection lifetime: both servers set only ReadHeaderTimeout of five seconds (cmd/gs/main.go:1721 and :1779) and no ReadTimeout, WriteTimeout or IdleTimeout, so a slow body and an idle keep-alive connection are bounded in size but not in time. That is exactly the slow-body condition the request names. Note that these bounds reached main without security/service-boundary-bounds (a63c378a) being an ancestor of it, so do not use that branch to judge what landed.\n\nBatch two, the remaining seven of that self-queue, follows separately."}